inbox has PRIMARY KEY (consumer, message_id). During a rebalance, two consumers briefly process the same message (READ COMMITTED):

A: BEGIN;
A: INSERT INTO inbox (consumer, message_id) VALUES ('cert-counters', 'm-77') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;   -- INSERT 0 1
B: BEGIN;
B: INSERT INTO inbox (consumer, message_id) VALUES ('cert-counters', 'm-77') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;   -- (waits)
A: UPDATE course_stats SET certificates = certificates + 1 WHERE course_id = 'sql-101';
A: COMMIT;
B:                                                                                            -- INSERT 0 0

Statement: "B's insert waited for A's uncommitted row with the same key and, once A committed, took the conflict path; the handler must treat INSERT 0 0 as a duplicate and skip the UPDATE."
